 "c": [
  {"i":4008,"t":["nature","home"],"n":"Fire and burning are a natural phenomenon, and 燃えるゴミ is taught in household garbage sorting. Burning is not a hand action."},
  {"i":4012,"t":["actions"],"n":"A general verb of replacing and switching. The link to work shifts is too loose for a work unit."},
  {"i":4030,"t":["communication"],"s":{"2":["sports"]},"n":"The core sense is a document, minutes or log. Sports applies only to the record-setting sense, so it goes in a sense entry."},
  {"i":4038,"t":["qualities","home"],"s":{"4":["character"]},"n":"Dirty and messy fit qualities and home. 汚い手/汚いやり方 ('underhanded') is a common N3 sense and is a character trait."},
  {"i":4039,"t":["school","work","character"],"n":"An effort expression taught with 頑張る for studying and working, and it describes a hardworking person. It is not a grammar word."},
  {"i":4049,"t":["work","routine"],"n":"A break is taught with the workplace and the daily routine. The time link is loose."},
  {"i":4115,"t":["time"],"n":"The adverb means 'for the first time in a while', so it is a time word. The greeting is the separate phrase お久しぶりです."},
  {"i":4129,"t":["character","language"],"n":"Polite and careful describe a person's manner. Polite speech (丁寧語, 丁寧な言い方) is taught in the language/keigo unit. The word is not a greeting phrase itself."}
 ],
 "d": [
  {"i":4026,"keep":[5],"n":"時間を潰す / 暇つぶし is a common N3 expression and fits a time unit"},
  {"i":4028,"keep":[],"n":"怒りが爆発する is a figurative extension, so it would not be taught in a feelings unit"},
  {"i":4030,"keep":[2],"n":"世界記録 and 記録を出す are common, and a teacher would teach them in sports"},
  {"i":4038,"keep":[4],"n":"汚い in the sense of 'underhanded' (汚いやり方, 汚い人) is common and describes a person's character"},
  {"i":4042,"keep":[],"n":"隙 as 'unguarded moment' is a situational lapse, not a personality trait, so character does not fit"},
  {"i":4053,"keep":[3],"n":"気分が沈む and 沈んだ顔 are common and belong with moods"},
  {"i":4061,"keep":[2],"n":"蚊に刺される and 蜂に刺される are very common and are taught with insects"},
  {"i":4066,"keep":[6],"n":"天気が崩れる is a standard weather-forecast phrase"},
  {"i":4075,"keep":[],"n":"なめるな in the sense of 'look down on' is slangy and would not be taught in a relationships unit"},
  {"i":4098,"keep":[],"n":"Learners meet 動揺 as emotional agitation; the physical-shaking sense is rare for them"},
  {"i":4103,"keep":[4],"n":"鬼 as 'it' in 鬼ごっこ / かくれんぼ is common and is taught with children's games"},
  {"i":4106,"keep":[1],"n":"携帯する / 携帯用 meaning 'carry on one's person' is a common N3 sense, separate from the phone"},
  {"i":4133,"keep":[4],"n":"山手線 and 2番線 are everyday railway words taught in transport"},
  {"i":4137,"keep":[],"n":"The core sense is 'refrain'; 'jot down' and 'be imminent' are secondary and would not be taught in the communication or time units"}
